{% extends "layout.njk" %}

{% from "govuk/components/panel/macro.njk" import govukPanel %}

{% block pageTitleContent %}Application submitted{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
  <div class="govuk-grid-row">
    <div class="govuk-grid-column-two-thirds">

      {{ govukPanel({
        titleText: "Application submitted",
        html: "Your mocked reference number<br><strong>" + referenceNumber + "</strong>"
      }) }}

      <h2 class="govuk-heading-m">What happens next</h2>

      <p class="govuk-body">
        In a real service, we would now review your application and be in
        touch. In this demo, nothing has actually happened: no email has
        been sent, no case has been created, and no data has left this
        local demo environment. The reference number above was generated
        entirely on this local server, purely so this page looks like a
        real GOV.UK confirmation page -- it does not correspond to any
        real application, and cannot be looked up anywhere.
      </p>

      <p class="govuk-body">
        Your answers from this journey have now been cleared from this
        demo's temporary, in-memory session. Refreshing this page, or
        starting the journey again, begins with a completely empty set of
        fictional answers.
      </p>

      <p class="govuk-body">
        <a class="govuk-link" href="/">Start another demo application</a>
      </p>

      <p class="govuk-body govuk-!-margin-top-6">
        DEMO -- not a live service. Not affiliated with, endorsed by, or
        representative of Defra or HM Government. This is a mocked
        confirmation only -- no real application was submitted, stored, or
        sent anywhere -- this page only demonstrates what a GOV.UK
        confirmation page for a converted paper form would look like.
      </p>

    </div>
  </div>
{% endblock %}
